[req] raw model output (1879 chars): "Two steps, in this order — the order matters:\n\n1. **Sign out inside OpenDesign** (Settings → Account → Sign out).\n2. **Then unbind the three projects** — while you're signed in, the app instantly re-creates the bindings every time the project list loads (`bindUnboundProjectsToPersonalWorkspace`), so the unbind only sticks *after* sign-out.\n\nI can do step 2 for you the moment you've signed out: it's one statement —\n\n```sql\nDELETE FROM workspace_projects;   -- in ~/Library/Application Support/Open Design/namespaces/release-stable/data/app.sqlite\n```\n\nNothing else is deleted: the projects table, files, conversations, and `workspace_artifacts` all reference `projects` directly, and all three bindings are `local_only` with no cloud resource ids — so the cloud has nothing that gets orphaned.\n\nWhy sign out **first**: right now all three are bound to the workspace. If you just quit the app without signing out and without unbinding, the local list will show **zero** projects (worse than before). After sign-out the re-binder stops running, the DELETE is permanent, and all three appear in the local list immediately — the renderer refetches `/api/projects` when you open the project view, so no"
