s/matching/scorer.ts` (ADDITIVE: new fn + exports only, existing symbols byte-identical) enumerating orgs with fresh/unscored lots and running the existing per-tenant scoring via `getAdminClient()`; call it at the end of `run.ts`'s ingest flow; keep `scripts/e2e-ingest.ts` imports unchanged-compatible; keep the ≥80 alert audit behavior; `tender_lot_matches` stays the write target. Persisting `combined_score` is §3 backlog — only if a trivial fit with existing columns.\n2. Persist exported artifacts: on successful compile ONLY, upload the artifact via service-role Supabase Storage (lazy `storage.api.upsert`/ensure private bucket `bid-exports`) and write the storage path into `bid_proposals.final_docx_path` scoped `.eq(\"org_id\", orgId)`; streaming response unchanged; gated (409) path writes nothing. If storage proves unclean, fall back to writing `final_docx_path` as a documented not-yet-persisted note — pick one, be honest in code comments.\n3. Caddyfile TLS conditional: apply `tls` (cert/key) only when cert files are present; when `deploy/certs/` absent (documented ACME mode `CADDY_TLS_CREDS=false`) let Caddy do ACME — Caddyfile env-var text substitution tricks (e.g. `tls {$CADDY_TLS_ARGS}` expansion or site-address tweaks) are fair game; default local-cert mode behavior unchanged; rest of file intact.\n4. Cron route: exempt EXACTLY `/api/cron/:path*` from the middleware session wall (matcher + body early-allow BEFORE the `if (!userId)` redirect; CRON_SECRET query gate remains the only check; missing secret ⇒ 401 as today). If deletion is cleaner (route is dead weight; §4 defers a real cadence scheduler), delete route + matcher entry instead — one or the other, documented in code.\n\nWRITE SCOPE: `src/services/gets/run.ts`, `src/services/matching/scorer.ts` (additive only), `src/services/export/compiler.ts`, `src/services/export/types.ts`, `src/app/api/bids/[bidId]/export/route.ts`, `src/app/api/cron/ingest-gets/route.ts` (or deletion), `src/middleware.ts` matcher