0c4ddc429e230a3bc1c1719f67e14324749df200a4b90` — lib-1/my-spec string was a 63-hex typo; compose file + commit message now byte-exact (attestation anchor). auth/rest/storage healthchecks probe-verified + `service_healthy` deps; api-gw listener-bind-only (envoy has no admin — residual). prod compose Caddy network-alias = split-DNS kill of the app↔DB public hairpin (browser origin unchanged). backup-cron.sh (BACKUP-FAILED/BACKUP-LAST-OK sentinels; cron/systemd alternatives in comments, nothing auto-installed) + check-backup-fresh.sh (26h staleness + sentinel; FR-304 interim alert interface = exit code; BSD/GNU stat bug self-caught, runtime matrix tested). observability.yml overlay UNWIRED + OBSERVABILITY.md honest inventory. root .gitignore += `deploy/state/`. Residuals: envoy admin/ready follow-up; node_exporter has no scraper; `INFERENCE_BIND_IP` must be an IP literal (pre-existing).\n- [!] Transport die-off #1: original U1/K1/G2 (des-1/fix-10/ora-4) died `FailedToOpenSocket` pre-write (tree audited clean; task_revive rejected their IDs) → fresh re-dispatch des-2 / ses_ef594ad0dffeY9yK14D8V4seuS, fix-11 / ses_ef594ad08ffekKGeAuiSyaA3oy, ora-5 / ses_ef594ad06ffez652DdkAxKZYA0. Die-off #2: fix-11 + ora-5 hit `FailedToOpenSocket` again; gen-7/gen-8 revivals show advancing last_activity (state running, terminal evidence unreadable) → NOT re-dispatched to avoid dual-writer on K1 scope. des-2 unaffected, RUNNING.\n- [x] README consolidation — DONE by orchestrator: backup-cron/check-backup-fresh ops, hairpin alias, observability overlay, sentinels folded into `deploy/README.md`; committed together with TODO §1/§6 ticks + deferred-§3 backlog (housekeeping commit).\n- [ ] Gates: G1 CLOSED. G2=ora-5 awaiting verdict (docs `6e222ef` vs memo; if transport kills it again → fresh oracle dispatch). G3 (wiring) pending des-2+fix-11 landing. G4 (readiness) dispatchable — all Phase 4 lanes terminal (T1 `2514236`, CI1 `39215ef`, INF1 `232e797`). Standing Phase-4 residuals: CI embeddin