entinel check; exit code = interim FR-304 alert interface); `deploy/observability.yml` overlay (explicitly UNWIRED — loopback Caddy admin, digest-pinned node_exporter + curl probe, log caps) + `deploy/OBSERVABILITY.md`; root .gitignore += deploy/state/.\n- The HEAD~1/HEAD~2 housekeeping commits (this turn): `deploy/README.md` consolidation (hairpin paragraph, Files table rows for the new scripts, Cadence section stating schedule NOT auto-installed + exit-code interim alerting, Observability section marking overlay unwired, dockerignore note) and TODO tracker ticks.\n\nVerify (in order of risk):\n1. Compose validity: `docker compose config` (NO sudo) parses for deploy/supabase/docker-compose.yml, deploy/docker-compose.prod.yml, deploy/cluster/docker-compose.inference.yml (inference compose has a pre-existing strict-parse requirement: INFERENCE_BIND_IP must be an IP literal — set a dummy env if needed; that quirk itself is NOT a finding). Healthcheck/depends_on graph: no service starts against an unhealthy dep; api-gw listener-bind limitation honestly commented.\n2. Backup scripts: read backup-cron.sh + check-backup-fresh.sh closely — sentinel write/clear logic (BACKUP-FAILED cleared on next success? BACKUP-LAST-OK only on exit 0?), 26h threshold math, stat portability (a BSD/GNU stat bug was found+fixed pre-commit — confirm the fix is real), exit-code contract matches README/OBSERVABILITY claims. Scripts are not auto-installed anywhere — confirm nothing silently schedules itself.\n3. CI: compliance-ci.yml job graph — gate.needs lists ALL blocking jobs (6 expected); integration-e2e genuinely applies the B3 migration `supabase/migrations/20261005000000_vault_rpc_tenant_boundary.sql` (or documented psql fallback) then re-runs the axe/login-guard assertions with REAL env (the §1 fail-closed middleware `bcd025f` must be what's asserted); build job's image actually starts (image-smoke); .dockerignore excludes (.next, node_modules, .env*, .git, deploy/certs) without breaking prod.Dockerfile COPYs (read the Dockerfile's COPY lines against it). deploy.yml: ghcr push + takahe-labeled runner pull; any secrets handling sane.\n4. Honesty audit: OBSERVABILITY.md + deploy/README.md must not claim anything unwired is wired (overlay, exporter scraping absent, alerting = exit codes, cron not installed, restore drill E-07 unverified). Flag overclaim as MATERIAL.\n5. Validation run in a HEAD worktree: `npm ci` is unnecessary if node_modules fine — just `npm run typecheck`, `npm run test`, `npm run lint` on the HEAD worktree (report raw results; pre-existing single copilot lint warning acceptable). If worktree setup is too heavy, run on main tree ONLY if git status shows clean src/ — otherwise skip and say so.\n\nOut of scope / accepted (don't re-litigate): the scoring formula, §1 security semantics (G1-CLOSED), §5 doc truth (G2), Phase 3 wiring gaps (U1/K1 in flight), need for live takahe runner, E-01/E-07 live-infra evidence deferrals, CI embedding stub being lexical-not-bge-m3 (recorded residual), 443-UDP optional, envoy has no admin endpoint (api-gw healthcheck honest limitation accepted).\n\nDeliverable: verdict APPROVE / APPROVE-WITH-FIXES / BLOCK; MATERIAL/MINOR findings each with file:line + what's wrong + why it matters. Explicitly list residual risks you accept. If you find a broken compose/CI parse or honesty overclaim, that's MATERIAL."})
